      "ReviewText": "Weekends used to feel like a battlefield: one arm wrestling a gas mower, the other juggling the toddler, grass clippings stuck to my face. Now? Friday night I just lift the 22-lb X3 PLUS out of the trunk—lighter than the cat-litter I hauled last week—tap “Start” on my phone, and it hums a little tune while it maps the yard.\nBefore work the next morning I schedule the “night shift” for 8 p.m. When I get home, the lawn looks like a hotel carpet, even the tricky fence line razor-sharp. The neighbor’s golden retriever barks like crazy; the mower flicks its tail and glides around him, leaving the dog frozen mid-bark.\nAt 10 p.m. I can still let it run—the noise is quieter than our kitchen dishwasher. Best part? The second the first raindrop falls, it scoots back to its dock in 30 seconds. When the sun returns, it finishes the job—no soggy clippings anywhere. The time I saved? Enough to build an entire Lego set with my kid.\nBottom line: this thing is cheaper—and way more reliable—than hiring a lawn service.",
